# Line endings here are not a matter of taste.
#
# The golden corpus under tests/golden is compared byte for byte against what
# the compiler emits, and the compiler emits LF. The .lime round-trip tests do
# the same. If git checked these out as CRLF - which it does by default on
# Windows - every one of those tests would fail on a fresh clone, for a reason
# that has nothing to do with the code.
#
# Lua 5.4 also rejects a UTF-8 BOM, which is why nothing here is ever written
# with one; see readLime/readScene.
* text=auto eol=lf
